🟡 **Suggestion - Defensive Programming**: The recursive pagination follows `next_page_id` without a depth limit. If the backend has a pagination bug (circular references), this could loop infinitely.

Practically unlikely, but adding a sanity check is cheap insurance:

```suggestion
async function fetchPage(
  provider: string,
  pageId?: string,
  depth = 0,
): Promise<LLMModel[]> {
  if (depth > 10) {
    throw new Error(`Too many pagination requests for provider ${provider}`);
  }
  const page = await ConfigService.searchModels({
    provider__eq: provider,
    limit: 100,
    page_id: pageId,
  });

  if (page.next_page_id) {
    const rest = await fetchPage(provider, page.next_page_id, depth + 1);
    return [...page.items, ...rest];
  }
  return page.items;
}
```

